{"componentChunkName":"component---src-pages-work-wp-portfolio-slug-jsx","path":"/work/facial-recognition/","result":{"data":{"wpPortfolio":{"title":"FACIAL RECOGNITION","content":"<p>In 2019, I was commissioned to make several iterations of a facial recognition system, which enabled users to log into a prototype application. The system was designed for both a kiosk and as a Progressive Web Application for a global brand. The users’ facial data was stored as a JSON object firstly within the application and subsequently in a Google Firebase database. If there was match between the user’s face on the camera and facial data in the system, then the application would allow the user to log in.</p>\n","slug":"facial-recognition","url":{"url":"https://github.com/pauljavascripting/facial-recogntion-demo"},"image1":{"image1":{"mediaDetails":{"sizes":[{"sourceUrl":"https://story-spinner-vvj7.temp-dns.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/face-recog1-148x300.png","width":"148","name":"medium"},{"sourceUrl":"https://story-spinner-vvj7.temp-dns.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/face-recog1-150x150.png","width":"150","name":"thumbnail"}]}}},"image2":{"image2":{"mediaDetails":{"sizes":[{"sourceUrl":"https://story-spinner-vvj7.temp-dns.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/face-recog2-148x300.png","width":"148","name":"medium"},{"sourceUrl":"https://story-spinner-vvj7.temp-dns.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/face-recog2-150x150.png","width":"150","name":"thumbnail"}]}}},"image3":{"image3":null},"image4":{"image4":null},"image5":{"image5":null}},"seoPage":{"nodeType":"Portfolio","title":"FACIAL RECOGNITION","uri":"/portfolio/facial-recognition/","seo":{"title":"FACIAL RECOGNITION - My Blog","metaDesc":"","focuskw":"","metaKeywords":"","metaRobotsNoindex":"index","metaRobotsNofollow":"follow","opengraphTitle":"FACIAL RECOGNITION - My Blog","opengraphDescription":"In 2019, I was commissioned to make several iterations of a facial recognition system, which enabled users to log into a prototype applicatio